    <text>
        <body>
            <div xml:id="d453">

                <pb facs="0673" n="657" sameAs="frus:frus1947v04/pg657"/>

                <note rend="inline" type="source">811.79661/2–1847: Telegram</note>
                <opener>
                    <seg rendition="#center">[Extract]</seg>
                </opener>
                <head>
                    <hi rendition="#italic">The Ambassador in the Soviet Union</hi> (<hi rendition="#italic">Smith</hi>) <hi
                        rendition="#italic">to the Secretary of State
                    </hi>
                </head>
                <opener>
                    <seg rendition="#float-left">
                        <hi rendition="#small-caps">secret</hi>
                    </seg>
                    <dateline rendition="#float-right">
                        <placeName>
                            <hi rendition="#small-caps">Moscow</hi></placeName>, <date
                            calendar="gregorian" when="1947-02-18T17:00:00+03:00">February 18,
                            1947—5 p. m.</date>
                    </dateline>
                </opener>
                <p rendition="#flush">434.</p>
                <p rendition="#center">. . . . . . . . . . . . . .</p>
                <p>I also brought up matter of the lend-lease settlement, pointing out that failure
                    of the Soviet Govt to reply to our repeated overtures was <pb facs="0674"
                        n="658" xml:id="pg658"/> becoming embarrassing to us. I stressed importance
                    of beginning these discussions and continuing them, even though they are
                    protracted. Vyshinski<anchor n="1" xml:id="d453-f1"/> assured me that he would
                    follow this through personally.</p>
                <closer>
                    <signed>
                        <hi rendition="#small-caps">Smith</hi>
                    </signed>
                </closer>
            </div>
        </body>
    </text>
    <standOff>
        <listAnnotation>
            <note corresp="#d453-f1" n="1" xml:id="d453-f1-content">
                <p>Andrey Yanuaryevich Vishinsky, Deputy Minister for Foreign Affairs of the Soviet
                    Union. This conversation probably occurred on February 15.</p>
            </note>
        </listAnnotation>
    </standOff>
